+# Nemotron Hyperdrive (trt-loop, 2026-11-02): NHD_GUIDED_SKIP=1. With guided decoding configured, every eager
+# (not CUDA-graph) step of one-model speculative decoding enqueues the grammar host functions and then waits on
+# the GPU (_drain_host_functions) after the target logits and after each draft step, 4 times per step, even when no
+# request in the batch is guided. Each wait empties the GPU queue, and the GPU then idles while the host launches
+# the next kernels (prefill and mixed steps, ~19 ms per 383 ms prefill step and ~16 ms per mixed step on B300).
+# For such a batch every one of those calls is a no-op (_build sets token_mask only for guided rows, so the bitmask
+# kernel leaves the logits unchanged, and the host functions only touch guided requests), so the step skips them.
+# It does so only when the previous step's guided calls also ran eagerly, so no host function of an earlier step
+# (a CUDA-graph host node) can still be pending while this step continues without draining; the first eager step
+# after graph replays keeps the stock path and drains them. Batches with a guided request always keep it.
+_NHD_GUIDED_SKIP = os.environ.get("NHD_GUIDED_SKIP", "0") == "1"
+
 
